  "problems": "",
  "rationale": "Setting --skip_markduplicates true disables the BAM_MARKDUPLICATES_PICARD subworkflow (use_rustqc is false, so validation passes), so the Picard and markdup-stats processes no longer run. Every genome-BAM consumer (StringTie, BAM_QC_RNASEQ tools, BEDTools coverage and the bigWig chain) now receives the coordinate-sorted STAR BAM instead of the markdup BAM, so these must rerun. MultiQC gets the ALIGN_STAR samtools stats instead of the markdup stats and Picard metrics, so it reruns too. Transcriptome-BAM Salmon quantification, DESeq2 and STAR_ALIGN are upstream of or independent from duplicate marking and are unchanged."
